WEBVTT

00:04.750 --> 00:09.240
I had never even dreamed 
of the sight I saw that day.

00:10.380 --> 00:13.370
Even now, after so, so long,

00:14.170 --> 00:16.950
my memory of it hasn't faded in the slightest.

00:18.010 --> 00:20.980
But how I've longed to see him,

00:21.490 --> 00:25.470
even if it were only in a dream...

00:27.030 --> 00:29.500
I miss him.

00:29.900 --> 00:31.370
I want to see him one more time...

00:44.140 --> 00:45.350
Am I...

00:45.350 --> 00:46.660
All right?

00:47.210 --> 00:48.460
Yes.

00:48.460 --> 00:50.710
More importantly, is Ms. Murasame...

00:51.130 --> 00:53.530
No, is Phantom nearby?

00:54.150 --> 00:56.590
She's nowhere in the vicinity.

00:56.590 --> 00:59.210
It would seem she's disappeared.

00:59.800 --> 01:02.190
That was too easy.

01:02.190 --> 01:05.930
Though a Spirit that's divided its power
too greatly wouldn't amount to much more.

01:07.460 --> 01:14.210
However, defeating Phantom doesn't 
mean I've achieved my goal.

01:14.880 --> 01:18.090
Yes, yes. Of course not.

01:18.090 --> 01:22.960
Our goal isn't the present fragmented fool.

01:22.960 --> 01:26.560
It's the monster of the past
at its full power.

01:26.980 --> 01:33.440
Still, why would Phantom divide 
her power to create more Spirits?

01:34.100 --> 01:37.970
She must have known that would 
inevitably spell her own decline.

01:39.820 --> 01:44.400
So you're saying Kurumi 
has saved you over 204 times?

01:44.400 --> 01:45.200
Yeah.

01:45.660 --> 01:47.280
Every time I got killed,

01:47.280 --> 01:51.090
she rewound time and stopped DEM's attack.

01:51.460 --> 01:55.020
Kurumi's goal is to go back in time 
and defeat the Spirit of Origin

01:55.020 --> 01:57.850
in order to save her best friend.

01:58.630 --> 02:03.720
She also means to prevent all tragedy 
caused by Spirits before it ever happens.

02:04.270 --> 02:07.510
And she needs my Spirit power to do that.

02:09.730 --> 02:13.630
I can't believe that's what was 
going on with Kurumi...

02:13.630 --> 02:15.990
I'm surprised.

02:16.330 --> 02:19.050
So even the Sephirah within each of us

02:19.050 --> 02:24.450
were refined at the cost of 
countless human lives...

02:24.450 --> 02:27.420
I have mixed feelings about that.

02:28.960 --> 02:31.500
Whatever Kurumi's reasons may be,

02:31.500 --> 02:34.350
we can't afford to hand over
 Shido's Spirit power.

02:34.350 --> 02:35.960
That comes above all else.

02:35.960 --> 02:37.120
For one thing,

02:37.120 --> 02:41.450
we don't have any guarantee that Kurumi 
can even defeat this Spirit of Origin.

02:41.450 --> 02:44.850
Her story's also hard for me to believe.

02:45.140 --> 02:49.910
That's right. You've fought Kurumi 
plenty of times already.

02:49.910 --> 02:50.370
But—

02:50.370 --> 02:51.350
Even so!

02:51.350 --> 02:56.680
If you ask me if it's <i>more</i> likely
 that you're lying to me, big brother,

02:56.680 --> 02:59.490
then I'm forced to believe you two 
by a narrow margin.

02:59.820 --> 03:01.900
This is getting complicated.

03:01.900 --> 03:04.990
Though I understand what you're getting at.

03:05.300 --> 03:07.120
More importantly, big brother,

03:07.120 --> 03:10.160
there's one other thing 
I'm very concerned about.

03:10.160 --> 03:11.000
Hmm?

03:11.000 --> 03:15.500
This Mio Takamiya woman 
that came up in your story.

03:15.940 --> 03:19.260
I find it hard to believe 
she's unrelated to you and me.

03:19.260 --> 03:21.390
If her last name really is Takamiya,

03:21.390 --> 03:25.620
then there's a chance she's family.
 A blood relative.

03:26.090 --> 03:27.890
I was curious about that too.

03:28.600 --> 03:31.400
Who is this Mio Takamiya?

03:31.400 --> 03:34.150
And what is she creating Spirits for?

03:34.580 --> 03:37.400
She gave Kurumi her Sephirah 
and made her a Spirit.

03:38.010 --> 03:41.900
Sounds like the Phantom 
that appeared before us.

03:42.320 --> 03:43.940
Mio Takamiya...

03:43.940 --> 03:45.150
Phantom...

03:45.150 --> 03:48.090
And the Spirit of Origin 
that Kurumi mentioned...

03:48.680 --> 03:49.710
Question.

03:49.710 --> 03:54.000
What is the relationship between all three?

03:55.630 --> 03:58.330
If only we could use my Raziel...

03:58.330 --> 04:01.040
Then we'd have our answer in an instant.

04:01.040 --> 04:04.300
Indeed, it's a peculiar story, but...

04:04.640 --> 04:07.640
If you're so curious,

04:07.640 --> 04:10.930
all you have to do is 
remember your past, right?

04:11.290 --> 04:13.560
If only I could.

04:14.380 --> 04:17.720
But both Mana and I have lost 
our memories.

04:18.180 --> 04:23.060
We don't even know a single 
thing about why we lost them.

04:23.060 --> 04:25.700
You told me that before.

04:26.110 --> 04:29.330
That's why I'm saying 
you should try remembering.

04:30.740 --> 04:32.710
You think I can?

04:32.710 --> 04:35.680
My Michael is an absolute key.

04:35.680 --> 04:37.710
There's nothing it can't open.

04:37.710 --> 04:42.460
Not even the door to your sealed memories.

04:44.460 --> 04:45.630
Hold on!

04:45.630 --> 04:47.720
Is it safe to do something like that?

04:47.720 --> 04:50.720
I don't know what happened in the past,

04:51.000 --> 04:52.890
but it won't harm Darling

04:52.890 --> 04:55.710
the moment he remembers, will it?

04:56.130 --> 04:57.130
Big brother...

04:57.670 --> 04:58.900
I'll be all right.

04:58.900 --> 05:00.110
Don't worry.

05:00.810 --> 05:03.110
This isn't just about
our connection to Mio Takamiya.

05:03.540 --> 05:06.110
I want to know what happened in our past

05:06.410 --> 05:09.270
more than anyone else.

05:11.090 --> 05:12.350
Shido...

05:13.290 --> 05:14.210
Michael!

05:19.220 --> 05:21.010
Okay, here I go.

05:21.010 --> 05:21.810
Yeah!

05:22.590 --> 05:24.140
Don't worry.

05:24.140 --> 05:26.050
Believe in Michael.

05:27.180 --> 05:30.690
Such a long, hard object is going into Darling!

05:30.690 --> 05:33.140
Miku, be quiet for a bit.

05:30.690 --> 05:33.870
No! You can't! Don't!

06:03.100 --> 06:06.380
Oh, you've awakened, Shin.

06:06.380 --> 06:07.380
Wha?!

06:07.640 --> 06:10.230
Hmm? Is something wrong?

06:11.010 --> 06:14.020
Oh, no, it's nothing.

06:14.460 --> 06:15.390
Shido!

06:16.210 --> 06:17.550
Are you okay?

06:17.550 --> 06:18.590
Shido!

06:18.590 --> 06:21.110
Please take it easy.

06:21.110 --> 06:23.170
What's this now?

06:23.170 --> 06:24.360
What's going on?

06:24.670 --> 06:26.570
What do you mean, "What's going on"?!

06:26.570 --> 06:29.380
You suddenly collapsed and gave us a fright!

06:29.380 --> 06:30.490
Agreed.

06:30.490 --> 06:32.960
After inserting Michael into your head,

06:32.960 --> 06:34.940
you passed out.

06:34.940 --> 06:35.660
Huh?

06:37.110 --> 06:39.500
I see. Sorry.

06:39.500 --> 06:41.230
Guess I worried you all.

06:41.230 --> 06:43.540
No, what matters is you woke up.

06:43.870 --> 06:45.400
I knew my kiss would work.

06:45.810 --> 06:47.310
It woke Sleeping Beauty.

06:47.310 --> 06:47.860
Huh?

06:48.550 --> 06:50.910
What nonsense are you spouting now?

06:50.910 --> 06:52.950
Don't listen to her, Shido.

06:52.950 --> 06:54.530
Wait a minute now.

06:54.530 --> 06:57.810
There are numerous particles
 floating in this space,

06:58.090 --> 07:03.090
so you can't say for certain that ones 
from my breath didn't reach Shido's.

07:03.440 --> 07:07.790
So I see no problem with regarding
 this as an indirect kiss.

07:07.790 --> 07:09.840
Hold it right there, Professor!

07:09.840 --> 07:14.700
That would mean that me and everyone 
in this same room have been...

07:15.070 --> 07:18.040
Deeply entwined in a deep kiss.

07:18.040 --> 07:20.720
I can't believe such genius lies here!

07:20.720 --> 07:23.670
What has the scientific world 
been doing this whole time?!

07:23.670 --> 07:27.160
Hold on. I'm not following now.

07:27.160 --> 07:29.370
Just how are we all entwined?

07:29.370 --> 07:31.810
I'll explain it in practice later!

07:31.810 --> 07:34.300
While Natsumi joins us for a three-way!

07:34.690 --> 07:37.470
Could you not rope me into this too?

07:35.020 --> 07:37.470
I'm sorry, Master.

07:37.470 --> 07:40.950
This was all because 
I suggested using Michael.

07:40.950 --> 07:44.290
Oh, no. Nothing's actually wrong.

07:44.290 --> 07:46.190
See? I'm just fine!

07:47.130 --> 07:48.690
Master...

07:48.690 --> 07:50.410
So, big brother,

07:50.410 --> 07:52.030
what happened?

07:52.030 --> 07:54.270
Did you remember anything?

07:54.270 --> 07:55.490
Well, I...

07:57.380 --> 07:59.450
Huh? That's odd.

07:59.780 --> 08:02.530
I'm certain I saw something.

08:03.020 --> 08:05.850
Yet I can't remember anything.

08:08.820 --> 08:11.290
There's no need to hurry, Shin.

08:12.020 --> 08:14.550
You can just think of another way.

08:15.390 --> 08:16.860
Reine...

08:16.860 --> 08:20.770
Then could you try it on me too, big brother?

08:20.770 --> 08:21.710
Huh?

08:21.710 --> 08:26.270
It might not have worked for you, 
but I might be able to remember something.

08:26.270 --> 08:29.260
Whether it's about Mio Takamiya

08:29.260 --> 08:32.010
or whatever happened to us in the past.

08:32.010 --> 08:32.850
Yeah, yeah.

08:32.850 --> 08:34.860
We'll try that later, okay?

08:34.860 --> 08:37.870
Right now, let's wait 
for Shido to recover first.

08:37.870 --> 08:38.850
Huh?

08:38.850 --> 08:40.530
What's the big idea?

08:42.580 --> 08:44.010
She's right.

08:44.010 --> 08:45.160
I'm sorry, Mana.

08:45.160 --> 08:46.920
Can we try it another time?

08:47.460 --> 08:48.370
Hmm?

08:51.580 --> 08:54.070
Ike, you said you found something?

08:54.550 --> 08:57.250
How has Nightmare, Kurumi Tokisaki,

08:57.250 --> 09:01.420
been able to interfere 
with every one of our attacks?

09:02.200 --> 09:06.760
She's been aware of our plans in advance.

09:07.160 --> 09:10.590
To be precise,
she's actually experienced them,

09:10.590 --> 09:13.610
then altered things each time

09:13.920 --> 09:17.360
to avoid Shido Itsuka's death.

09:17.360 --> 09:18.190
What?

09:18.740 --> 09:21.290
That would spell trouble.

09:21.780 --> 09:24.440
It means we'll always be a step behind.

09:24.440 --> 09:25.550
Indeed.

09:26.060 --> 09:28.590
Though we're not necessarily
at a disadvantage.

09:29.500 --> 09:32.530
Any strategy we conduct several times,

09:32.530 --> 09:35.170
Nightmare will have to face 
several hundred times.

09:35.510 --> 09:39.730
Repeating the same thing 
over and over will exhaust her mind.

09:39.730 --> 09:45.640
Even Nightmare can't have 
endless stamina and willpower.

09:46.100 --> 09:50.310
Are you suggesting we wait 
until Nightmare gives up?

09:51.010 --> 09:53.400
That's our most certain option.

09:53.660 --> 09:56.500
However, there's still a chance

09:56.500 --> 10:01.510
Nightmare could come up with 
some solution we won't be able to think of.

10:01.510 --> 10:04.370
So we should also do everything in our power

10:04.370 --> 10:07.540
to ensure she gives up as soon as possible.

10:10.070 --> 10:12.180
Father, Father!

10:12.180 --> 10:13.380
Look, look!

10:13.380 --> 10:14.920
We caught this.

10:15.340 --> 10:16.680
Nightmare!

10:16.680 --> 10:18.450
Eavesdropping, huh?

10:18.450 --> 10:20.440
Well done, Nibeelcole.

10:21.080 --> 10:24.600
But several people she was with got away.

10:24.600 --> 10:28.310
They might have overheard your conversation.

10:28.310 --> 10:30.360
What's wrong with that?

10:30.360 --> 10:34.530
Let's have an all-out war with full knowledge
 of each other's capabilities.

10:35.190 --> 10:37.900
There's still at least one of you left, right?

10:38.400 --> 10:40.820
Tell your master for me...

10:41.330 --> 10:45.510
I <i>will</i> kill Itsuka Shido.

10:46.080 --> 10:49.500
No matter how many times you go back in time.

10:49.500 --> 10:52.250
No matter how often you redo this world

10:52.760 --> 10:56.200
or how often you rewrite history.

10:56.200 --> 11:00.060
I'll be so thorough that
there's no overturning it.

11:00.680 --> 11:03.710
Now, struggle all you like,

11:04.930 --> 11:07.320
vilest Spirit.

11:12.810 --> 11:16.610
I was relieved Mana 
backed down for us yesterday.

11:16.610 --> 11:20.360
She had her magic power
 enhanced by DEM, after all.

11:20.660 --> 11:22.930
If she'd recalled those memories too,

11:22.930 --> 11:25.210
it would have been pretty damaging.

11:25.210 --> 11:28.370
Even if we want intel on Mio Takamiya.

11:28.730 --> 11:30.860
Mio Takamiya, huh?

11:32.190 --> 11:33.560
<i>I wonder why...</i>

11:33.560 --> 11:37.270
<i>I feel sure I've known 
that name for a long time now.</i>

11:42.680 --> 11:43.960
Kurumi!

11:43.960 --> 11:48.010
Good day, Shido, Kotori.

11:48.300 --> 11:50.050
Good morning, Kurumi.

11:50.050 --> 11:53.050
You're wearing an awfully 
nice outfit today, aren't you?

11:53.050 --> 11:54.270
It's her clone.

11:55.020 --> 11:56.910
Thank you for last night.

11:56.910 --> 11:58.440
I should thank you.

11:58.440 --> 12:02.430
But it's still too early for you
 to be thanking me.

12:02.430 --> 12:03.160
Huh?

12:03.560 --> 12:09.410
On February 20th, DEM Industries 
will use their full forces

12:09.820 --> 12:12.130
to come kill you, Shido.

12:13.730 --> 12:17.170
I came here today to warn you of that.

12:19.370 --> 12:21.800
So, what's your objective?

12:23.180 --> 12:24.410
To be honest,

12:24.410 --> 12:30.930
the main body of Kurumi Tokisaki doesn't 
know that I, her clone, am here right now.

12:31.500 --> 12:37.270
The real me intends to handle 
this matter all on our own.

12:37.700 --> 12:40.820
She plans to repeat time as often as it takes

12:40.820 --> 12:44.410
to seize a future in which Shido survives.

12:45.070 --> 12:49.670
However, our enemy is aware of her resolve.

12:49.670 --> 12:52.010
That's why they're using their full forces.

12:52.010 --> 12:54.080
DEM's operation

12:54.080 --> 12:59.690
is also an attempt to break my spirit 
as I pass through time.

13:00.810 --> 13:06.470
So the real reason you're here is 
to encourage Shido to evacuate?

13:06.470 --> 13:09.970
That alone is not the entirety of the truth.

13:09.970 --> 13:10.720
Huh?

13:11.400 --> 13:14.690
It would be a waste for Shido 
to remain in the dark

13:14.690 --> 13:20.690
when I'm working so hard 
to protect him, wouldn't it?

13:22.390 --> 13:23.610
I get it.

13:26.700 --> 13:28.450
Now, if you'll excuse me.

13:28.450 --> 13:32.080
Please do survive this, Shido.

13:32.380 --> 13:33.070
Kurumi!

13:33.770 --> 13:36.080
Yes, what is it?

13:36.360 --> 13:39.580
If it's possible, tell Kurumi:

13:40.020 --> 13:43.830
"Thank you. I'm still alive because of you.

13:44.370 --> 13:47.470
But I won't be the one 
in need of saving forever.

13:47.790 --> 13:51.930
Once we've taken care of DEM, 
I'll come to seal your Spirit power—"

13:52.830 --> 13:54.060
No, that's not right.

13:55.300 --> 13:59.180
"This time, I'll be the one to steal a kiss.

13:59.900 --> 14:02.500
So prepare yourself, my honey."

14:09.110 --> 14:11.740
What a wonderful retort.

14:12.170 --> 14:15.000
I'm truly blessed.

14:30.640 --> 14:32.300
Wednesday, February 15th

14:30.760 --> 14:32.300
You have a new message.

14:32.300 --> 14:33.010
Kotori

14:32.300 --> 14:33.010
Today

14:32.300 --> 14:33.010
Reine, come to the meeting room
We have an emergency.

14:33.550 --> 14:35.800
You're coming, Wizard?

14:36.940 --> 14:38.890
The situation is dire.

14:39.410 --> 14:40.800
Judging from the state of things,

14:40.800 --> 14:44.520
the information we received from 
Kurumi's clone is worth believing.

14:44.930 --> 14:48.970
Though we also can't afford 
to run and hide forever.

14:48.970 --> 14:51.920
But there's no negotiating either.

14:51.920 --> 14:52.660
Certainly.

14:53.000 --> 14:55.160
There's no room for discussion here.

14:55.540 --> 14:56.670
Which means...

14:56.670 --> 14:58.290
We only have one option left.

14:58.750 --> 15:00.540
Defeating DEM.

15:01.850 --> 15:03.790
Of course, that's easier said than done.

15:04.170 --> 15:07.170
But we'll have to go on the offensive

15:07.800 --> 15:10.330
in order to seize our own future.

15:10.330 --> 15:12.910
<i>That's right, Commander Itsuka.</i>

15:13.300 --> 15:14.670
Mr. Woodman!

15:15.560 --> 15:18.200
Are you feeling better already?

15:18.200 --> 15:21.810
<i>Yes, you don't need to worry about me.</i>

15:22.090 --> 15:25.500
<i>I'm sorry I was out of contact for so long.</i>

15:26.890 --> 15:29.550
<i>Our enemy is certainly great.</i>

15:29.550 --> 15:34.760
<i>However, DEM is an organization helmed</i>

15:34.760 --> 15:39.700
<i>by Isaac Westcott's charisma 
and Ellen Mathers's competence.</i>

15:39.700 --> 15:45.840
<i>That means it won't be much of a threat 
once those two are taken out.</i>

15:46.110 --> 15:50.570
In other words, defeating Westcott 
and Ellen is our key to victory.

15:51.210 --> 15:52.520
<i>Understood.</i>

15:52.520 --> 15:55.970
<i>Then perhaps it would be worth trying </i>that<i>.</i>

15:55.970 --> 15:57.030
Huh?

15:57.030 --> 15:59.100
MARIA, what do you mean by "that"?

15:59.100 --> 16:04.350
<i>I'm saying that it might be 
possible to nullify Nibeelcole.</i>

16:04.350 --> 16:05.160
Huh?!

16:05.640 --> 16:09.370
Truthfully, I also have an idea 
for how to handle Bandersnatch.

16:09.370 --> 16:10.610
H-Hold on!

16:10.610 --> 16:12.100
The enemy's new Realizer models are—

16:12.100 --> 16:13.620
Stop, stop!

16:13.620 --> 16:15.120
Enough talking about it.

16:15.520 --> 16:17.460
<i>What's the matter, Nia?</i>

16:17.460 --> 16:19.620
<i>We're just getting to the main topic.</i>

16:19.620 --> 16:21.150
Tsk, tsk, tsk.

16:21.150 --> 16:23.850
You don't get it, Robo-girl.

16:23.850 --> 16:27.250
<i>First, I demand an explanation 
for that nickname.</i>

16:27.250 --> 16:29.750
<i>Depending on your answer, 
I may eject you from the ship.</i>

16:29.750 --> 16:31.170
Have you forgotten?

16:31.170 --> 16:34.380
Westcott can use Beelzebub, 
the omniscient Demon King.

16:34.380 --> 16:35.140
Ah!

16:35.500 --> 16:36.760
That's right.

16:36.760 --> 16:40.380
He can look up any event that happens 
throughout the entire universe.

16:40.380 --> 16:41.910
Meaning...

16:41.910 --> 16:46.020
He might learn everything 
that unfolds in this discussion.

16:46.020 --> 16:47.850
Exactly.

16:47.850 --> 16:48.780
However,

16:48.780 --> 16:51.480
it doesn't know how to read people's minds

16:51.480 --> 16:53.560
or what the future holds.

16:53.560 --> 16:55.860
So even if you come up with a strategy,

16:55.860 --> 16:57.910
you can't mention it out loud.

16:58.580 --> 17:00.890
<i>I hate to admit it, but you are correct.</i>

17:01.250 --> 17:02.980
<i>Thank you, Nia.</i>

17:05.160 --> 17:06.970
As long as you understand!

17:06.970 --> 17:08.670
Humility is a virtue,

17:09.180 --> 17:11.380
spriteless Robo-girl.

17:12.010 --> 17:15.960
<i>By the way, Nia, could you 
please touch my console?</i>

17:15.960 --> 17:17.300
Huh? Like this?

17:22.550 --> 17:24.770
Hey! What are you doing?! Come on!

17:24.770 --> 17:27.370
<i>I'm grateful for the flaw you pointed out.</i>

17:27.370 --> 17:32.520
<i>However, you needed to be punished 
for that insulting nickname.</i>

17:33.320 --> 17:35.280
That's false logic!

17:35.570 --> 17:38.260
Still, it's rather absurd that we have to have

17:38.260 --> 17:42.060
our strategy meeting without being 
able to voice any ideas or opinions.

17:42.060 --> 17:44.700
I think there are still things 
we can each do on our own.

17:45.180 --> 17:47.170
There's something I'd like to take care of, too.

17:47.170 --> 17:48.690
<i>Good point.</i>

17:48.690 --> 17:51.670
<i>I'll do everything I can as well.</i>

17:56.050 --> 17:58.580
Do you have any excuse for yourself?

17:58.580 --> 17:59.840
My, oh my.

18:00.220 --> 18:03.600
I already received word from another me.

18:03.880 --> 18:09.350
I heard you informed Shido 
and Kotori about DEM's assault.

18:09.670 --> 18:13.780
I can't have you acting on your own 
without orders from me.

18:14.420 --> 18:19.060
You'll need to pay for disturbing 
the order with your life.

18:19.720 --> 18:23.490
Yes, yes. There's no getting past that.

18:24.850 --> 18:26.460
But one last thing.

18:27.240 --> 18:29.620
I have a message from Shido.

18:31.130 --> 18:35.090
"I love, love, super-love you! 
Let's get married, my honey!"

18:35.090 --> 18:38.260
Only the "my honey" part of that was accurate!

18:39.860 --> 18:43.960
I know you already heard it 
from another clone.

18:51.880 --> 18:53.670
My, oh my.

18:54.300 --> 18:55.700
I wouldn't be so foolish

18:55.700 --> 18:58.970
as to pare down my own forces 
right before a major battle.

18:59.280 --> 19:02.200
If you are still a part of me,

19:02.200 --> 19:04.030
then at least be useful first

19:04.520 --> 19:06.790
and then die on the battlefield for me.

19:09.770 --> 19:14.310
Yes, yes. I understand.

19:15.950 --> 19:19.300
A secret organization protecting Spirits, huh?

19:19.640 --> 19:21.450
You show up out of nowhere,

19:21.450 --> 19:23.430
and you expect us to believe that nonsense?

19:23.430 --> 19:25.310
B-But Captain,

19:25.310 --> 19:29.140
they've both come here 
knowing it meant great danger.

19:29.140 --> 19:32.440
I don't think we should be 
so quick to assume they're lying.

19:32.440 --> 19:35.330
I know you must find it hard to believe.

19:35.330 --> 19:38.760
But it's all true.

19:38.760 --> 19:40.110
On February 20th,

19:40.110 --> 19:43.320
there will likely be a major 
battle here in Tengu City.

19:43.650 --> 19:44.670
When it goes down,

19:44.670 --> 19:48.670
DEM will probably request 
even the captains sortie.

19:49.340 --> 19:51.710
But I want you to ignore that request.

19:52.090 --> 19:57.320
Is that also information uncovered 
by the secret organization Ratatoskr?

19:57.320 --> 20:00.410
Still, even if what you say is true...

20:00.410 --> 20:01.220
That's right.

20:01.530 --> 20:06.600
Spurning DEM's request means 
ignoring orders from above.

20:06.980 --> 20:11.640
So you're asking us to lose our jobs 
and serve prison time on top of that?

20:11.640 --> 20:12.940
For one thing,

20:13.330 --> 20:16.670
why are you telling us 
not to attack the Spirits?

20:16.670 --> 20:18.480
They're the enemy of mankind, aren't they?

20:18.480 --> 20:22.750
That's maliciously spun 
information spread by DEM.

20:22.750 --> 20:26.200
The Spirits have no intention 
of attacking mankind.

20:27.740 --> 20:30.590
That's a lot to take in all at once.

20:32.350 --> 20:34.940
If what you just told us is true,

20:34.940 --> 20:39.610
then I would love to try fiddling with this 
secret organization's new weapons!

20:39.610 --> 20:41.840
It's stirring my instincts as a mechanic!

20:41.840 --> 20:44.130
Sorry, but could you be quiet for a bit?

20:48.290 --> 20:50.890
You know we can't do what you're asking.

20:51.280 --> 20:52.810
Captain...

20:52.810 --> 20:53.900
That's a shame.

20:53.900 --> 20:56.150
Though I don't fault you for your decision.

20:56.420 --> 20:59.300
Still, if you do deploy to the battlefield,

20:59.300 --> 21:00.980
at least stick to the rear.

21:00.980 --> 21:01.530
Huh?

21:02.310 --> 21:04.030
I don't want to kill you all.

21:05.030 --> 21:07.250
Sounds like you're really
underestimating us.

21:07.250 --> 21:09.120
I know you were a skilled fighter, but...

21:12.050 --> 21:12.950
Please.

21:29.120 --> 21:31.350
Zaphkiel, Het!

21:31.580 --> 21:32.180
Het!

21:32.430 --> 21:33.430
Het!

21:33.680 --> 21:34.560
Het!

21:34.560 --> 21:40.320
Het, Het, Het, Het, Het, Het,

21:40.670 --> 21:41.660
Het!

21:47.240 --> 21:52.950
Now, shall we begin our Date?

21:52.950 --> 21:54.950
<b>Episode 1</b>

21:52.950 --> 21:54.950
<b>Beginnings of War</b>

23:24.960 --> 23:39.980
Episode 2   "Final Respite"

23:25.830 --> 23:28.440
The big battle against DEM draws near,

23:28.440 --> 23:30.510
with everyone harboring different feelings

23:30.510 --> 23:32.440
as they spend what time remains.

23:32.840 --> 23:35.470
Next time is episode 2, "Final Respite."

23:35.970 --> 23:38.910
The curtain rises on <i>Date A Live</i> season 5!
